# BuildKit honours <dockerfile>.dockerignore (this file) IN PREFERENCE to a
# context-root .dockerignore. Patterns are relative to the BUILD CONTEXT ROOT,
# which for this Dockerfile is the PARENT of the loom repo (/home/devuser/workspace)
# — a huge tree (~160 entries, all of ruvector's ~120 crates, node_modules, VMs).
# So we ALLOWLIST: ignore everything, then re-include ONLY loom/ and the single
# ruvector-core crate the facade path-depends on. Last match wins.

# 1) Ignore every top-level entry in the parent context.
*

# 2) Re-include the two trees we vendor.
!loom
!ruvector

# 3) Trim ruvector down to just the core crate (drop the other ~120 crates,
#    examples, node bindings, .git, the real 120-member root — the Dockerfile
#    COPYs our trimmed workspace root over it instead).
ruvector/*
!ruvector/crates
ruvector/crates/*
!ruvector/crates/ruvector-core
ruvector/crates/ruvector-core/target
ruvector/crates/ruvector-core/**/*.rvdb

# 4) Trim the vendored loom of build output, VCS, and heavy non-build assets.
#    (app/data + data ARE kept — the smoke stage bakes the real generation.)
loom/target
loom/.git
loom/.github
loom/uplift-results
loom/bench/out
loom/bench/results
loom/legacy
loom/model
loom/tests/target
loom/.agentic-qe
loom/.claude-flow
loom/node_modules
loom/**/__pycache__
loom/**/*.pyc
loom/**/.DS_Store
loom/**/*.log
